  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-csv-viewer",
      "text": "DSH Web plugin that adds a `dsh-better-sidebar` viewer for `.csv` and `.tsv` files."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Run this in the environment where DSH Web is installed:\n\n```powershell\ndsh plugin --profile web add https://github.com/hi-wenw/dsh-csv-viewer.git\n```\n\nRestart DSH Web, then hard-refresh the browser with `Ctrl+Shift+R`. Open a CSV or TSV file from the sidebar to use the viewer."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- automatic delimiter detection for comma, tab, semicolon, and pipe-separated files;\n- virtualized rows, so large tables do not create one DOM node for every row;\n- sticky header and source row numbers;\n- case-insensitive content search;\n- numeric/text column sorting with ascending, descending, and reset states;\n- `Table` / `Raw` preview modes;\n- CSV quoting, escaped quotes, CRLF, and quoted newlines."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```powershell\npnpm install\npnpm build\npnpm check\n```\n\nThe DSH client bundle is generated at `lib/client.js`. The host entry is `lib/index.js` and the bundle registration is in `cordis.patch.yml`."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
